From: Mikhail Mlhcnn <mikhail@advnirr.org>
Subject: [PATCH] udfps: hold a configurable refresh rate while the overlay is shown

Touching the fingerprint sensor on degas brightens the whole screen whenever the
display mode changes while local HBM is lit. Measured on hardware: with nothing
changing the mode (already at 144 Hz, no other voter) a touch lights only the
spot; with the refresh rate pinned to 120 Hz the per-touch UDFPS vote switched
the panel 120 -> 144 under the lit sensor, and every such touch flashed.

The per-touch vote is the problem. UdfpsController asks DisplayModeDirector
for the highest refresh rate on every finger down (UdfpsTouchOverlay.
configureDisplay -> UdfpsDisplayMode.enable -> PRIORITY_UDFPS, the top
priority) and drops it on finger up, so every press is a potential mode change
exactly while LHBM is on. On top of that the panel driver runs LHBM at 120 Hz
and reprograms the DDIC there, so on a 144 Hz display the vote also leaves DRM
and the panel disagreeing about the rate.

Stock HyperOS does it the other way round. libmisurfaceflinger's
FodMonitorThread::updateLHBMFodFlag() enters FOD on ENROLL_START/AUTH_START:
forceSkipIdleTimer(true) and changeFps(ro.vendor.display.fod_monitor_default_fps
= 120); it leaves on ENROLL_STOP/AUTH_STOP with forceSkipIdleTimer(false) and
changeFps(0). The rate is fixed for the whole session and never touched under
the finger.

Mirror that:

* config_udfpsRefreshRate (default 0 = unchanged behaviour). When set,
  DisplayModeDirector's UDFPS vote asks for that rate, if the display has a
  mode for it, instead of the highest one.
* UdfpsController takes the vote when the overlay is shown - the AOSP
  equivalent of a started enroll/auth session - and releases it when the
  overlay is hidden. The vote pins the physical rate, so the display does not
  idle down to 60 Hz in between either, like forceSkipIdleTimer.
* On a touch it signals UI ready straight away, as with config_ignoreUdfpsVote,
  instead of configuring the display per press.
diff --git a/core/res/res/values/config.xml b/core/res/res/values/config.xml
index fbe4c3280..c8881c82c 100644
--- a/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -3441,6 +3441,12 @@
     <!-- When true, udfps vote is ignored. This feature is disabled by default. -->
     <bool name="config_ignoreUdfpsVote">false</bool>
 
+    <!-- Refresh rate, in Hz, to hold for the whole time the UDFPS overlay is shown, instead of
+         voting for the highest refresh rate on every touch. For panels whose local HBM runs at
+         a fixed rate and which flash when the display mode changes while it is lit. 0 keeps the
+         default per-touch vote for the highest refresh rate. -->
+    <integer name="config_udfpsRefreshRate">0</integer>
+
     <!-- Controls if local secondary displays should be private or not. Value specified in the array
          represents physical port address of each display and display in this list will be marked
          as private. {@see android.view.Display#FLAG_PRIVATE} -->
diff --git a/core/res/res/values/symbols.xml b/core/res/res/values/symbols.xml
index c3ef35717..743c5d1de 100644
--- a/core/res/res/values/symbols.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/values/symbols.xml
@@ -448,6 +448,7 @@
   <java-symbol type="bool" name="config_localDisplaysMirrorContent" />
   <java-symbol type="bool" name="config_allowPresentationOnInternalDisplay" />
   <java-symbol type="bool" name="config_ignoreUdfpsVote" />
+  <java-symbol type="integer" name="config_udfpsRefreshRate" />
   <java-symbol type="bool" name="config_enableProximityService" />
   <java-symbol type="bool" name="config_enableVirtualDeviceManager" />
   <java-symbol type="array" name="config_localPrivateDisplayPorts" />
